# Plain language for market-pilot dashboard

## Audience

Assume the reader is new to trading bots and Jev. Avoid jargon unless you define it once in simple words.

## When explaining features (chat or docs)

- Lead with **what it does for them**, not implementation (no PostgREST, backfill timers, etc. unless they ask).
- Separate **live behavior** (“what the bot uses now”) from **analytics** (“what happened later”).
- Use short paragraphs and tables for compare/contrast (e.g. calibration vs min confidence).
- Say what the feature does **not** do (e.g. calibration does not retrain Jev or change trades by itself).

## When writing frontend descriptions

Match existing patterns in `dashboard/components/settings-form.tsx`:

- **`SETTING_DESCRIPTIONS`**: one line, ~8–15 words, scannable under the label.
- **`SETTING_DESCRIPTIONS_FULL`**: 1–2 sentences, “you” voice, concrete consequence (fewer trades, pickier, etc.).

Rules for new copy:

- Prefer **“the bot”** / **“Jev”** over internal names (`return_15m_pct`, `forward_returns_checked_at`).
- Use **percent** for probabilities users see in UI (85%), not decimals (0.85), unless the input is explicitly a decimal field.
- Chart/helper text under titles: `text-xs text-zinc-500`, one idea per sentence, optional second sentence for “what to do if empty/wrong.”
- Empty states: say **why** (e.g. “waiting for older predictions to mature”) and **what will appear**, not “no data.”
- Do not promise profit; use “tended to,” “on average,” “sanity check,” “near-miss.”

## Trading terms (use consistently)

- **Min Jev confidence** — lowest BUY % required before the bot may open a trade.
- **Calibration** — after the fact: did higher BUY scores match better 15m price moves?
- **Watchlist** — symbols Jev monitors; different threshold than trade entry (`watchlist_min_buy`).

## Do not

- Wall of acronyms without definition.
- Duplicate long paragraphs in both short and full description unless the full one adds real detail.
- Imply backfilled returns feed back into live Jev API calls (they do not in this codebase).
